Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: restore SM8750 bonded slave clock state

The SM8750 slave PHY selects the external bit clock, but still has its own
pixel divider and clock mux. A PHY reset clears those registers. Saving and
restoring only the clock master leaves the slave's hardware state different
from the common clock framework's cached rates.

On Piano at 120 Hz, post-clock register capture shows CMN_CLK_CFG0=0x51
on both PHYs at first boot. After DPMS off/on the master stays at 0x51,
but the slave becomes 0xf1 and immediately reports VID_MDP FIFO overflow.
Its local PLL DECIMAL_DIV_START_1 also changes from 0x1f to 0x41.

Opt SM8750 into saving and restoring the slave's existing PLL/divider
state through the same lifecycle as the master. Keep other PHY variants'
restore policy unchanged. No divider value or display mode is hardcoded.

Piano register capture confirms both dividers return to 0x51 after DPMS
off/on. The previous FIFO fault no longer occurs during the 120 Hz
off/on cycle or 60/120/90/144/120 Hz modeset sequence.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy.h
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@
 	const int quirks;
 	bool has_phy_regulator;
 	bool has_phy_lane;
+	/* Bonded slave has independently reset divider/mux registers. */
+	bool restore_slave_pll;
 };
 
 extern const struct msm_dsi_phy_cfg dsi_phy_28nm_hpm_cfgs;
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy.c
@@ -781,7 +781,8 @@
 	 * link clocks. Restore PLL status if its PLL is being used as clock
 	 * source.
 	 */
-	if (phy->usecase != MSM_DSI_PHY_SLAVE) {
+	if (phy->usecase != MSM_DSI_PHY_SLAVE ||
+	    phy->cfg->restore_slave_pll) {
 		ret = msm_dsi_phy_pll_restore_state(phy);
 		if (ret) {
 			DRM_DEV_ERROR(dev, "%s: failed to restore phy state, %d\n",
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
@@ -440,6 +440,9 @@
 
 	/* Save PHY status if it is a clock source */
 	msm_dsi_phy_pll_save_state(msm_dsi->phy);
+	if (is_bonded_dsi && msm_dsi1 &&
+	    msm_dsi1->phy->cfg->restore_slave_pll)
+		msm_dsi_phy_pll_save_state(msm_dsi1->phy);
 
 	/* Keep the clock-source host running until the bonded slave's link
 	 * clocks have stopped. Match the reverse power-on order and the
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -1541,6 +1541,7 @@
 
 const struct msm_dsi_phy_cfg dsi_phy_3nm_8750_cfgs = {
 	.has_phy_lane = true,
+	.restore_slave_pll = true,
 	.regulator_data = dsi_phy_7nm_98000uA_regulators,
 	.num_regulators = ARRAY_SIZE(dsi_phy_7nm_98000uA_regulators),
 	.ops = {
